{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (recorded by orchestrator): Option 2 — REMOVE the prefix field from both consumers, simplifying both KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS tables to a bare int. Rationale (operator + orchestrator analysis): the feature is unused-but-wired with no live row using a prefix and no honest coverage (the 84c7-era assertion is vacuous with every live prefix empty); repo policy prefers deleting unused code over adding tests for an unused feature; a future prefixed helper can re-add the field with real coverage at that point. Scope: strip the prefix element from the row tuples in scripts/gen_env_registry.py and scripts/check_config_ownership.py, drop the 'prefix + lit' application code in _scan_call and _helper_access, update tuple-shape-touching tests; docs/env-vars.md must be unchanged (no live row used a prefix). This resolves the design fork escalated in the previous comment; description AC will be rewritten to this chosen fork before plan review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787345637776702001,"uuid":"c7146430-8ff6-4b29-82b8-6b5c346910d5"}